title: First day — meetings, the probe, the cover story
story: ides-of-march
author: Sharpee Platform
seed: 42
description: First-meeting greetings for all three principals; Burbage's
  identity probe grips the reply over his own same-key topic row; after
  the exchange closes the same words fall through to the table; the
  cover story lands as a told claim; the play-book is guarded while the
  poet sits over it; steering the talk to the book gets noticed. A
  conversation holds one live scene at a time, so each principal gets
  the previous scene's decay before the next knock.
  Run: node dist/cli/sharpee.js --test
    --story stories/ides-of-march/chord/ides-of-march.story
    stories/ides-of-march/tests/transcripts/first-day.transcript

---

# The clown first: first-meeting boundary row.
> talk to kemp
[OK: contains "A new face among the hired men"]

# His grievance, plainly asked — this threads the offer later.
> ask kemp about the grievance
[OK: contains "SET DOWN"]

# Norwich before the story has traveled: the idle variant.
> ask kemp about norwich
[OK: contains "a town that knows how to laugh"]

> north
[OK: contains "Stage"]

# Let the clown's scene close before knocking on the tragedian.
> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

# Burbage's first-meeting row opens the identity probe.
> talk to burbage
[OK: contains "I do not know your face"]

# The gripped answer wins over his own norwich table row (the probe
# holds the floor), and the exchange closes on the served row.
> ask burbage about norwich
[OK: contains "the provinces keep better discipline"]

# The table serves normally after the exchange closed.
> ask burbage about the house
[OK: contains "worth a peg"]

# Same words again: the table row now, not the exchange.
> ask burbage about norwich
[OK: contains "So you said"]

# The claim proper: told to Burbage, witnessed, and his to spread.
> tell burbage about norwich
[OK: contains "Norwich"]

> west
[OK: contains "Tiring-House"]

# The tragedian's scene decays before the poet's opens.
> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> wait
[OK: contains "Time passes"]

> talk to shakespeare
[OK: contains "The new hired man"]

# Kemp not yet discussed with the poet: the quiet variant.
> ask shakespeare about kemp
[OK: contains "The yard loves him"]

# The book is guarded while he sits over it.
> take the play-book
[OK: contains "a half-second before yours"]

# Steering the talk from Kemp to the book gets marked as steering,
# and the plain question opens on its heels.
> ask shakespeare about the book
[OK: contains "You steer"]

# The gripped jest answer: he serves it and quits the scene.
> ask shakespeare about a spy
[OK: contains "given in jest"]
